cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
title: Antecedent
abstract: >-
  Antecedent is an identification-first causal inference engine for Python and
  Rust. It takes an analysis from causal structure through estimation,
  diagnostics, interventions, and counterfactuals — without silently treating
  discovered graphs as ground truth.
authors:
  - family-names: Hinshaw
    given-names: Charles
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-2421-4351"
  - name: Antecedent Contributors
version: 0.5.1
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.21556247
date-released: "2026-08-18"
url: "https://github.com/iridae-dev/antecedent"
repository-code: "https://github.com/iridae-dev/antecedent"
# CFF 1.2.0 cannot express the SPDX expression "MIT OR Apache-2.0"; the list is
# the schema-valid spelling of the dual license. Zenodo accepts neither form
# (zenodo/zenodo#2515) — the string→list→string flip-flop in bfb6144/ccafe22 each
# fixed one consumer while breaking the other. Zenodo now reads .zenodo.json
# instead and ignores this file entirely, so this file serves only CFF-schema
# consumers (GitHub's citation widget, cffconvert). Keep .zenodo.json present.
license:
  - MIT
  - Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - causal inference
  - identification
  - Bayesian inference
  - graph discovery
  - counterfactuals
identifiers:
